Plan 12 General Documentation

Plan 12 Developer Port Guide
Documentation version 1.1


Plan12 is a very open operating system. We like a lot of variety in our systems. The guidelines for what plan12
is defined as is well... not very strict. 

This article will discuss how to become a maintainer of a plan12 port and what all of that entales.



A maintainer is someone who manages, creates, and develops a port of plan12 to another architecture, 
microarchitecture, or philisophical standpoint. 
Plan12 simply has to fall under a few basic requirements to be officially published.

1. it must fall under the definition established in pre-2.4
2. it must maintain a small set of utilities with the same syntax

Once all of these are met, the plan12 port the reader is developing will be published officially.

Plan12 is defined as "A plan12 system is defined as a system that manages process spawning, killing, communication, data storage, and
permissions via filesystem abstractions in a numeric hiearchy - processes are designed to be first-class above
all else, turning all syscalls and process management into simple I/O operations."

This is the definition of plan12. Any system that can be described in this way IS plan12.


There are four major utilities to a plan12 system
All plan12 systems must ship with these utilities in the default installation or bootstrap tutorial.

EDIT - editor utility
Syntax - EDIT {LINE|HEX} {(item)}

Arg1 item HEX edits the selected item as a hexadecimal file.
Arg1 item LINE edits the selected item as an ASCII encoded file.

Arg2 is the path of the item to edit - since everything in plan12 is simply a file, this means EDIT can be
used to edit more than just text or files - it can also be used to write data to disks, perform process operations, 
and a lot more.

This is a very versatile utility, by design.


MOVE - item copy and deletion tool
Syntax - MOVE {(item)|REMOVE} (item)

Arg1 REMOVE removes the item at Arg2
Arg1 (item) copies the contents of Arg1 to Arg2

Arg2 being the item to enact on

This item is used to copy, move, and delete items and files in a plan12 system.


ASSEMBLE - basic assembler and linker binary
Syntax - ASSEMBLE (item)

Arg1 is the source code to assemble into an executable binary. The item after being assembled is 
named to assemble.out at the same path as the binary assembled. 


